  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. It is worth the usual 100100100 points in all divisions. Here, you need to solve the problem only for the entire array.**\n\nFor an array BBB containing MMM **distinct** integers, say [B1,B2,…,BM][B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_M][B1​,B2​,…,BM​], we define f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the number of distinct integers XXX that satisfy the following conditions:\n\n\nX≥1X \\ge 1X≥1; and\nThere exists 1≤i&lt;j≤M1 \\le i &lt; j \\le M1≤i&lt;j≤M such that it is possible to form a non-degenerate triangle with side lengths (Bi,Bj,X)(B_i, B_j, X)(Bi​,Bj​,X).\n\nA non-degenerate triangle is one with positive area.\nYou are given an array AAA containing NNN distinct integers. Find f(A)f(A)f(A).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the size of the array\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line one integer: f(A)f(A)f(A).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Ai≠AjA_i \\ne A_jAi​=Aj​ whenever i≠ji \\ne ji=j",
      "The sum of NNN across all tests does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
